SPOILERS!?

What you really need is to have either Excalibur or Stormbringer enchanted
to +8. I find this usually takes care of the Wiz in about 4 or 5 hits.
This is even more effective if you have speed boots (which you definitely
should have), since he will only hit you two or three times in the time it
takes to kill him. A bit better armour class would be handy too.
As you say, teleporting takes care of the pet problem. Even better is a ring of
conflict, since the Wizard's own pets will start putting shit on him (not in
corridors). A ring of regeneration is good too when fighting the hoards.
I've never used a wand of death on the wizard, but I've never thought it
necessary since a decent weapon makes pretty short work of him anyway.
And as other posters mentioned, it can be dangerous or ineffective.
Also, assuming you have telepathy, when he teleports away to get his breath
back, chase him. Teleport after him and keep hacking away.
Lastly, if he steals the amulet back off you after you get it and teleports
away, don't worry. He'll be back soon enough and you can kill him again.

Since you mention save files and dieing several times, I assume you are
backing up save files. While I think there is nothing wrong with this
(no more arguments/flames on this subject please :-), what often happens is
you end up trying to fight the wizard with a character possibly not well
equipped or strong enough, who would have died long before at the hands of
various nasties (particularly Minotaurs), but for copied save files.
I'm not suggesting this is necessarily the case, but if after another half
a dozen deaths you still haven't got anywhere, start a new game, and next time
you will know what you will need to properly handle him before you get there.

